## Clause 5. Goods and services that may be subject of preferred supplier contracts under section 366 (Optical goods and services)
Unofficial consolidated version of the Direction in relation to the preferred supply of goods and services-- as at 2 March 2026
5
Goods and services that may be subject of preferred supplier contracts under section 366 (Optical goods and services)
For the purposes of section 366 of the Act, I determine that MSD may enter into contracts on behalf of the Crown for the supply of the following goods and services for the purposes specified in section 367(2)(b) and (c) of the Act
Goods
(a)
spectacle frames;
(b)
spectacle lenses;
(c)
contact lenses;
(d)
ready to wear spectacles;
(e)
spectacle protection cases;
(f)
spectacle care products;
Services
(g)
eye examinations;
(h)
fitting of any goods listed in paragraphs (a) to (c);
(i)
fitting of any goods listed in paragraph (b) to frames supplied by the purchasers;
(j)
adjustment of any goods listed in paragraphs (a) and (d).

## Approval dated 18 March 2013
Unofficial version of the Special Needs Grants Programme - Approvals granted for rural assistance
## Approval for rural assistance under Special Needs Grants Programme
- Under clauses 18.2 and 18.6 of the Special Needs Grants Programme, as established and approved on 18 December 1998 under section 124(1)(d) of the Social Security Act 1964 (the programme), I give my approval for Part 6 of the programme to apply as follows:
Rural Assistance - Farmers
1.
Farmers in the affected areas whose primary industries are directly affected by drought are eligible to be considered for financial assistance under Part 6 of the programme.
2.
In relation to such farmers, Part 6 of the programme applies for the period beginning on 15 March 2013 (being the date on which the Minister for Primary Industries declared an adverse climatic event) and ending with the close of 30 September 2013, unless further extended by the Minister.
3.
In this approval, affected areas means-
(a)
the territories of the following local authorities:
(i)
Gisborne District Council;
(ii)
Horowhenua District Council;
(iii)
Manawatu District Council;
(iv)
Rangitikei District Council;
(v)
